      "summary": "Cardrona is open for skiing today, with cold conditions and fresh snow creating great skiing and riding across the mountain. The current report shows -3°C, 31 km/h winds with 53 km/h gusts, and 115 cm natural snow depth at 1,800m. Winds are easing, with clear skies expected to improve through the morning. The resort says snow coverage is at an all-time high for the season, with good conditions across the mountain. All 10/10 lifts are open, including McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express, Willow’s Quad, Wells Pipe Platter, Kindy Conveyor and Learner Conveyors. The report shows 9/10 terrain areas open, with Main Basin, Captains, Soho, Little Willows, Big Willows, Mt Cardrona, Arcadia Chutes, Learners Slopes and Ski Touring Access open. Summit is closed. The T-Bar is open, with Main Basin and Valley View scheduled from 8:30am, Captains from 9am, and Soho and Willows from 9:45am. The resort notes filming on Valleyview from 12–1pm, which may cause intermittent stops. The access road is chain free, although chains must be carried, and an active road hazard advisory remains in place. Carparks C, The Yard, Valley View and The Pines have availability, while A and B are full. The mountain is also hosting Green Steam x POW Day and live music today, with a POW Scavenger Hunt from 10am–1pm. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 10 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
