      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, with clear, sunny conditions and lovely overnight grooming setting up a strong day on the mountain. The latest report shows -2°C, 16 km/h winds with 31 km/h gusts, and 143 cm natural snow depth at the Home Basin weather plot. The resort reports fantastic coverage, with good groomed pistes and wind-loaded pockets available. Conditions in the Saddle are windswept in places. All 3/3 lifts are open: Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter. 11/11 listed groomed trails are open, including Main Street, Roller Coaster, Raffil's Run, Bullet, Pete's Treat, High Street, Side Saddle, Saddle Back and South Ridge. Current terrain status shows Home Basin, Powder Bowl, Saddle Basin, Summit Slopes, Backcountry Access, Skinning Access and Beginner Platter open, while Matukituki Basin and Motatapu Chutes are on hold. The report also confirms all lifts are open. The access road is chain free, but all vehicles must carry chains, with a free shuttle from the bottom of the access road. A road-hazard advisory remains active, and bikers are cautioned that the road is narrow in places. Today is Green Steam x POW Day, with live music and a POW Scavenger Hunt from 10am–1pm. Tomorrow brings Atomic Rise & Shine, the TC Interfields Ski Race and Out in The Alps Retro Dress Up Day. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
